title: Presidential Election
subtitle: Hindenburg runs for re-election...
view-if: year = 1932 and (month = 4 or month = 5) and presidential_election_seen = 0
frequency: 1000
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: schwesig_campaign = 0; hitler_support_hindenburg = 0; presidential_election_seen = 1; afd_candidate = "Hitler" if hitler_deported == 0 else afd_candidate = "Göring";
tags: event
go-to: election_algorithm
set-jump: pres_election
face-image: img/hindenburg_election.jpg

@pres_election

The presidential election is coming up soon. [? if spd_in_government = 0 : While the position of Chancellor is typically more important, recent governments have depended on the president's emergency decree powers, making the office vital. ?] [? if hitler_deported==0 : The Nazis will run Hitler, while the KPD will run Thälmann. A victory for Hitler would mean the end of parliamentary democracy, and the beginning of an era of unspeakable horrors. ?][? if hitler_deported==1 : Since Hitler has been deported, the Nazis will run Hermann Göring in his stead. He is widely seen as a proxy for Hitler, who, despite his legal persecution, retains a popular base who wishes to see him returned to Germany. Meanwhile, the KPD will run Ernst Thälmann. ?]
[? if sapd_formed: The SAPD, our former leftists, are supporting Thälmann of the KPD, and will likely share an endorsement with the Communists. ?]

# if hitler is deported, who would nsdap run? Duesterberg? or Goering?
# Goering runs, essentially as a proxy for Hitler, who is now stateless.

Many are calling for us to support the incumbent Hindenburg, despite his well-known reactionary tendencies. Is he truly the best bulwark against Hitler's ascension? On the other hand, many in our party are calling for Otto Braun to run again, but he is reluctant.

[? if linke_relation >= 50 : Another strange possibilty is an united front with the Communists, either to support Thälmann or our own candidate. ?]


- @support_hindenburg: Support Hindenburg.
- @support_schwesig: Run Otto Braun of the SPD.
- @support_thalmann: Support Ernst Thälmann of the KPD.

@support_hindenburg
subtitle: This is the default option.

Despite his known reactionary nature, Hindenburg has at least been keeping the Nazis at bay. Thus, we must support him.

- @final_election: The final vote...

@support_schwesig
subtitle: This will cost us 2 resources.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; schwesig_campaign = 1
go-to: schwesig_campaign

It takes effort to run a somewhat unexpected campaign. First, Braun has to be convinced to run. He himself had supported voting for Hindenburg, and it takes a good deal of prodding to convince him of his destiny.

The miniscule remnants of the Democratic Party (now called the German State Party) will likely support us. Who else will? Can we convince the Center to support Braun? What about the Communists?


@support_thalmann
choose-if: linke_relation >= 50 and reformist_strength < left_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if linke_relation < 50 : We do not have good enough relations with the Communists, so they are not even willing to accept our support. ?] [? if reformist_strength >= left_strength : The reformist faction is able to dissuade the party from supporting this arrangement. ?]

Supporting Thälmann is rather unpopular in our party, even if the Communists accept our support. Are we sure?

- @support_thalmann_2: Yes, we will support Thälmann, despite the reformists' pleas against it.
- @support_schwesig: Support Braun instead.
- @support_hindenburg: Support Hindenburg instead.

@support_thalmann_2
on-arrival: spd_support_thalmann = 1; reformist_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 10; rentner_spd -= 5; workers_spd -= 3; linke_relation += 10; communist_coalition += 2; union_relation -= 15; fdp_relation -= 15; gruene_relation -= 10

Fine. We have thrown our support to Chairman Thälmann of the KPD.

- @final_election: The final vote...

@schwesig_campaign

- @convince_union: Convince the Center Party.
- @convince_linke: Convince the Communists.
- @convince_liberals: Convince the remaining liberals, wherever they are.
- @final_election: The final vote...

@convince_union
choose-if: spd_votes >= union_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The Center knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
on-arrival: {!
Q.union_support_schwesig = 0;
if (Q.union_relation >= 55 || (Q.union_relation > 35 && Q.union_party_leader == "Joos")) {
    Q.union_support_schwesig = 1;
} else if (Q.union_relation <= 35) {
    Q.union_support_schwesig = 0;
} else {
    Q.union_support_schwesig = 2;
}
!}
go-to: union_failed if union_support_schwesig = 0 or (union_support_schwesig == 2 and historical_mode); union_success if union_support_schwesig = 1; union_partial if union_support_schwesig = 2 and not historical_mode
max-visits: 1

We remind the Center leaders of Hindenburg's anti-Catholicism, and try to convince them that Hindenburg's path will eventually lead to Hitler. We also remind them of the successes they've had as part of the Weimar coalition in Prussia with Otto Braun, and our support for the Center candidate Wilhelm Marx in the 1925 presidential election.

@union_success
go-to: schwesig_campaign

The Center are convinced! They will be part of the Braun coalition.

@union_partial

The Center are not satisfied with our arguments, but they are open to being convinced. They are willing to run a joint campaign if we front the resources.

- @pay_union: Give them the resources they need.
- @schwesig_campaign: Forget about the Center.

@pay_union
choose-if: resources >= 3
subtitle: -3 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 3)
on-arrival: resources -= 3; union_support_schwesig = 1
go-to: schwesig_campaign

With our resources, the Center are convinced to support Braun over Hindenburg.

@union_failed
go-to: schwesig_campaign

Unfortunately, we fail to turn them away from Hindenburg.

@convince_linke
choose-if: spd_votes >= linke_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The KPD knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
max-visits: 1

The KPD is supporting their own candidate, Ernst Thälmann. [? if linke_relation >= 50 : However, they are willing to be convinced to drop their campaign and support Braun; how do we convince them? ?][? if linke_relation < 50 or linke_party_leader != "Conciliators" : They do not seem willing to be convinced. ?]

- @linke_resources: Use our resources.
- @linke_relations: Use our good relations.
- @schwesig_campaign: Forget about the KPD.

@linke_resources
view-if: linke_relation >= 50 and not historical_mode
choose-if: resources >= 3
subtitle: -3 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 3).
on-arrival: resources -= 3; linke_support_schwesig = 1
go-to: schwesig_campaign

The KPD now endorses Braun in the presidential election! We ask them to keep their support low-key, so as to not alienate the bourgeois voters.

@linke_relations
view-if: linke_relation >= 60 or (linke_party_leader == "Conciliators" and linke_relation >= 45)
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations are not good enough.
on-arrival: linke_support_schwesig = 1
go-to: schwesig_campaign

The KPD now endorses Braun in the presidential election! We ask them to keep their support low-key, so as to not alienate the bourgeois voters.



@convince_liberals
max-visits: 1
go-to: convince_liberals_success if fdp_relation >= 50; convince_liberals_fail if fdp_relation < 50

The liberal vote ([+ gruene_name +] and DVP) has been falling over time, so they will probably be of minimal help to us. For what it's worth, the [+ gruene_name +] is already willing to support Braun.

@convince_liberals_success
on-arrival: fdp_support_schwesig = 1
go-to: schwesig_campaign

Thanks to our good relations, the DVP has promised to support Braun in the election.

@convince_liberals_fail
on-arrival: fdp_support_schwesig = 0
go-to: schwesig_campaign

We failed to convince the DVP to support Braun.



@final_election
on-arrival: election_round = 0
go-to: election_algorithm
set-jump: post_election


@post_election
on-arrival: {!
Q.schwesig_votes = 0;
Q.hindenburg_votes = 0;
Q.hitler_votes = 0;
Q.thalmann_votes = 0;

// initial phase:
Q.hitler_votes += Q.afd_normalized;
Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.other_normalized;
Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.bsw_normalized;

if (Q.schwesig_campaign) {
    Q.schwesig_votes += Q.spd_normalized;
    Q.schwesig_votes += Q.gruene_normalized;
    if (Q.union_support_schwesig && Q.union_support_schwesig == 1) {
        Q.schwesig_votes += Q.union_normalized;
    } else {
        Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.union_normalized;
    }
    if (Q.linke_support_schwesig) {
        Q.schwesig_votes += Q.linke_normalized;
        if (Q.sapd_formed && Q.sapd_votes) {
            Q.schwesig_votes += Q.sapd_normalized;
        }
    } else {
        Q.thalmann_votes += Q.linke_normalized;
        if (Q.sapd_formed && Q.sapd_votes) {
            Q.thalmann_votes += Q.sapd_normalized;
        }
    }
    if (Q.fdp_support_schwesig) {
        Q.schwesig_votes += Q.fdp_normalized;
    } else {
        Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.fdp_normalized;
    }
} else if (Q.spd_support_thalmann) {
    Q.thalmann_votes += Q.linke_normalized;
    Q.thalmann_votes += Q.spd_normalized;
    Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.union_normalized;
    Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.gruene_normalized;
    Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.fdp_normalized;
} else {
    Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.spd_normalized;
    Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.union_normalized;
    Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.gruene_normalized;
    Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.fdp_normalized;
    Q.thalmann_votes += Q.linke_normalized;
}
if (Q.hitler_support_hindenburg) {
    Q.hitler_votes -= Q.afd_normalized;
    Q.hindenburg_votes += Q.afd_normalized;
}

if (Q.hindenburg_to_schwesig_bonus) {
    Q.hindenburg_votes -= Q.hindenburg_to_schwesig_bonus;
    Q.schwesig_votes += Q.hindenburg_to_schwesig_bonus;
}
if (Q.thalmann_to_schwesig_bonus) {
    Q.thalmann_votes -= Q.thalmann_to_schwesig_bonus;
    Q.schwesig_votes += Q.thalmann_to_schwesig_bonus;
}

// check for majority
Q.hindenburg_votes = Math.round(Q.hindenburg_votes*1000)/10;
Q.schwesig_votes = Math.round(Q.schwesig_votes*1000)/10;
Q.hitler_votes = Math.round(Q.hitler_votes*1000)/10;
Q.thalmann_votes = Math.round(Q.thalmann_votes*1000)/10;

Q.hindenburg_majority = (Q.hindenburg_votes >= 50);
Q.thalmann_majority = (Q.thalmann_votes >= 50);
Q.hitler_majority = (Q.hitler_votes >= 50);
Q.schwesig_majority = (Q.schwesig_votes >= 50);
Q.any_majority = Q.hindenburg_majority | Q.thalmann_majority | Q.hitler_majority | Q.schwesig_majority;

// check for plurality
Q.hindenburg_plurality = (Q.hindenburg_votes >= Q.hitler_votes && Q.hindenburg_votes >= Q.schwesig_votes && Q.hindenburg_votes >= Q.thalmann_votes);
Q.thalmann_plurality = (Q.thalmann_votes >= Q.hindenburg_votes && Q.thalmann_votes >= Q.schwesig_votes && Q.thalmann_votes >= Q.hitler_votes);
Q.hitler_plurality = (Q.hitler_votes >= Q.hindenburg_votes && Q.hitler_votes >= Q.schwesig_votes && Q.hitler_votes >= Q.thalmann_votes);
Q.schwesig_plurality = (Q.schwesig_votes >= Q.hindenburg_votes && Q.schwesig_votes >= Q.hitler_votes && Q.schwesig_votes >= Q.thalmann_votes);
// If no candidate gets above 50%, then there's a second round. In the second round, a plurality wins. 
Q.election_round += 1;

// making the vote numbers nicer for the display
Q.hindenburg_votes_disp = Q.hindenburg_votes.toFixed(1);
Q.schwesig_votes_disp = Q.schwesig_votes.toFixed(1);
Q.hitler_votes_disp = Q.hitler_votes.toFixed(1);
Q.thalmann_votes_disp = Q.thalmann_votes.toFixed(1);
!}
go-to: hindenburg_wins if hindenburg_majority == 1; thalmann_wins if thalmann_majority == 1; hitler_wins if hitler_majority == 1; schwesig_wins if schwesig_majority == 1; no_majority_round1 if any_majority == 0 and election_round == 1; round2_results if election_round >= 2

Results:

Hindenburg - [+ hindenburg_votes_disp +]%

[+ afd_candidate +] - [+ hitler_votes_disp +]%

[? if linke_support_schwesig == 0 : Thälmann - [+ thalmann_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if schwesig_campaign > 0 : Braun - [+ schwesig_votes_disp +]% ?]

@no_majority_round1
on-arrival: hitler_support_hindenburg = 1 if (schwesig_plurality or thalmann_plurality)
go-to: round2_menu

There is no majority in this round. In the second round, any candidate who wins a plurality will win overall. What should we do?

[? if schwesig_plurality or thalmann_plurality : In order to consolidate the vote for the Right, and to prevent a socialist from becoming president, [+ afd_candidate +] is no longer running in the second round, and has switched his endorsement to Hindenburg. ?]


@round2_menu

- @round2_convince_union: Convince the Center to switch their support to us.
- @round2_convince_linke: Convince the KPD to switch their support to us. 
- @round2_hindenburg: Switch our support to Hindenburg.
- @round2_thalmann: Switch our support to Thälmann of the KPD.
- @round2_vote: Let the second round voting begin.


@round2_convince_union
view-if: schwesig_campaign > 0 and union_support_schwesig != 1 
choose-if: spd_votes >= union_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The Center knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
on-arrival: {!
Q.union_support_schwesig = 0;
// if Hindenburg support is greater than Hitler and Braun support, this should be much harder

if ((Q.union_relation >= 55 && Q.schwesig_votes >= Q.hindenburg_votes) || (Q.union_relation > 35 && Q.union_party_leader == "Joos")) {
    Q.union_support_schwesig = 1;
    if (Q.hitler_support_hindenburg) {
        Q.hindenburg_to_schwesig_bonus += Q.other_normalized/2;
    }
} else if (Q.union_relation >= 50 && Q.hitler_support_hindenburg) {
    Q.union_support_schwesig = 1;
    Q.hindenburg_to_schwesig_bonus += Q.other_normalized/2;
} else if (Q.union_relation <= 35 || (Q.union_relation <= 45 && Q.schwesig_votes < Q.hindenburg_votes && Q.hindenburg_votes > Q.hitler_votes && Q.difficulty >= 0)) {
    Q.union_support_schwesig = 0;
} else {
    Q.union_support_schwesig = 2;
}
!}
go-to: r2_union_failed if union_support_schwesig = 0 or (union_support_schwesig = 2 and historical_mode); r2_union_success if union_support_schwesig = 1; r2_union_partial if union_support_schwesig = 2 and not historical_mode
max-visits: 1

@r2_union_success
go-to: round2_menu
on-departure: hitler_support_hindenburg = 1 if schwesig_votes + union_votes > hitler_votes

[? if hitler_support_hindenburg : The Center's opinion is affected by the Nazis' support of Hindenburg, and is willing to turn away from him. ?] The Center are convinced! They will be part of the Braun coalition. [? if hitler_support_hindenburg : In addition, they will also bring in some minor parties who will support us. ?]

[? if not hitler_support_hindenburg and schwesig_votes + union_votes > hitler_votes: With the Center Party supporting Braun, [+ afd_candidate +] has dropped out of the race, and the Nazis have endorsed Hindenburg to prevent a socialist from becoming president. ?]

@r2_union_partial

The Center are not satisfied with our arguments, but they are open to being convinced[? if hitler_support_hindenburg: , especially given the Nazis' support for Hindenburg. ?]. They are willing to run a joint campaign if we front the resources.

- @r2_pay_union: Give them the resources they need.
- @round2_menu: Forget about the Center.

@r2_pay_union
choose-if: resources >= 2
subtitle: -2 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 2)
on-arrival: resources -= 2; union_support_schwesig = 1
on-departure: hitler_support_hindenburg = 1 if schwesig_votes + union_votes > hitler_votes
go-to: round2_menu

With our resources, the Center are convinced to support Braun over Hindenburg.

[? if not hitler_support_hindenburg and schwesig_votes + union_votes > hitler_votes: With the Center Party supporting Braun, [+ afd_candidate +] has dropped out of the race, and the Nazis have endorsed Hindenburg to prevent a socialist from becoming president. ?]

@r2_union_failed
go-to: round2_menu

Unfortunately, we fail to turn them away from Hindenburg. [? if hindenburg_votes > schwesig_votes : Given that Hindenburg received more votes than Braun, they believe that we should turn to Hindenburg, not the other way around. ?]




@round2_convince_linke
choose-if: spd_votes >= linke_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The KPD knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
view-if: schwesig_campaign > 0 and linke_support_schwesig == 0 
max-visits: 1

The KPD is committed to supporting Ernst Thälmann. [? if linke_relation >= 45 : However, the Nazi-Hindenburg coalition worries them enough that they are willing to be convinced to drop their campaign and support Braun. ?][? if linke_relation < 45 : They do not seem willing to be convinced. ?]

- @r2_linke_resources: Use our resources.
- @r2_linke_relations: Use our good relations.
- @round2_menu: Forget about the KPD.

